# Ignore build outputs from performing a nix-build or `nix build` command
result
result-*

# Ignore automatically generated direnv output
.direnv

# Claude Code writes accepted permission grants here. Its sibling
# .claude/settings.json is tracked (shared config), so the directory is already
# in the repo and this file would otherwise ride along into a repo attendees
# clone.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python track venv (created by `just setup-python`)
.venv/

# --- Language tracks ---
# All tracks are ignored up front, even though Exercise 3 is pick-one:
# trying another language is an extension exercise, and spare ignore
# rules cost nothing. This is the book's "step zero" principle applied —
# which is why the workshop skips the git step: it's already done here.

# Rust
# Source: https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Rust.gitignore (trimmed)
# Pulled: 2026-08-08
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

